remembering a young life lost too soon  sunday august 29 marking one year since  leslie palacio's death the man accused  of killing her eric rangala barra still  on the run tonight sally jeremiah spoke  to the family of the 22 year old who say  there isn't a day that goes by that they  don't think about her  i feel like every anniversary that comes  up i feel like i'm  really those moments again and it's just  horrible being here with the house quiet  it makes me feel so empty inside kaylee  palacio one of leslie's younger sisters  says despite a year going by it feels  just like yesterday when her family got  the news and her world turned upside  down it went by  super fast  and you know like everyone  is out here you know  with their siblings and  having a fun time when i'm over here you  know grieving and the grief unbearable  at times i miss her very much the family  describes leslie as independent  hard-working and always positive she's a  great person  and that she taught me some so much  stuff and a role model to kaylee i'm not  going to stop helping people because i'm  doing it for her i'm doing in her memory  i want people to remember her in a  positive way by caring for one another  most importantly i don't want her name  to be forgotten kaylie along with her  family attorney ophelia marcarion have a  message for the community keep following  the case to keep leslie's spirit alive  to know that we're not going to stop  it's been really really hard knowing  that it's been a year  and eric rangel is still out on the  streets i'm just not done  i don't know over here with me anymore  may she rest in peace sally caramillo 8  news now  while eric rangelabara has yet to be  captured his dad jose rangel was  recently sentenced to two years behind  bars for being an accessory to murder  for destroying evidence in that case
 

